course: dictionary
lesson: 303
title: Anagrams: the same letters, a new word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An anagram is a word or phrase made by mixing up all the letters of another word. «Listen» is an anagram of «silent», because both have the same letters, just in a different order.
explain: Every letter must be used exactly once. «Night» gives «thing», and «earth» gives «heart». If you miss a letter or add an extra one, it is not an anagram.
explain: Anagrams can be whole phrases too. «Dormitory» is an anagram of «dirty room», so spaces and capital letters do not count, only the letters do. When you solve an anagram puzzle, try moving the letters around until a real word appears.
fact: An anagram is a word or phrase made by rearranging all the letters of another word or phrase.
fact: «Listen» is an anagram of «silent»; «tinsel» and «enlist» are anagrams of it too.
fact: «Dormitory» is an anagram of «dirty room».
fact: Anagrams train your spelling and your thinking, and crosswords and word games use them.
fact: In maths, the number of ways to arrange the letters of «cat» is 3 × 2 × 1 = 6.
exercise: Which word is an anagram of «earth»? | table | happy | *heart
exercise: Which word uses all the letters of «night» in a new order? | sleep | *thing | nightly
exercise: «Dirty room» is an anagram of which word? | ROOM | tomorrow | *dormitory | DIRTY
test: What is an anagram of «cat»? | tack | *act | cot | dog
test: Which rule must an anagram follow? | Use only the vowels | You can add extra letters | *Use every letter exactly once | You can leave out letters
exam: In maths, how many ways can the letters of «cat» be arranged? | *6 | 9 | 12 | 3
